==============================================================================
   n | v2(T_n^cube) | clearing K3_n = 8 sum i^3 | margin v2(T) - (mu_bar-1) L K3_n (Y3 map)
   1 |           10 (law 10) |                        0 |       10.0
   2 |          140 (law 140) |                        8 |      105.9
   3 |          570 (law 570) |                       72 |      262.9
   4 |         1480 (law 1480) |                      288 |      251.8
   5 |         3050 (law 3050) |                      800 |     -361.7
   6 |         5460 (law 5460) |                     1800 |    -2216.4
   7 |         8890 (law 8890) |                     3528 |    -6155.7
   exact law (proved, note section 2.3): v2(T_n^cube) = L(3n^3 - 3n^2 + n), attained by the
   anti-diagonal permutation alone (no Cauchy-Binet cancellation), checked above.
   v2(T_n^cube) grows like 3 L n^3 while the clearing is 2 n^4 (quartic): the margin is
   negative from small n on, for every mu_bar > 1. The cube tails are not exponential sums in s
   (factor (rho^(3m))^(s^2)), so Cauchy-Binet gives no rank gain.

