==============================================================================
  signed two-family tails (= Euler's function): v2(T_n) = L[sum g_i + 2 sum (n-i) e_i] for n <= 9: True
  leading terms (5/8) L n^3 against a clearing 2 n^3 log2 M0: naive threshold mu_bar < 21/16 = 1.3125;
  the q-exponential representation (E1) is strictly better (3/2), and the unsigned sum has no
  single q-exponential representation (it is a product of three q-Pochhammer symbols).

