  The large gcds are the calculable defect of a NON-CANONICAL representation (non-primitive period,
  non-minimal preperiod: factors (2^|v|-M_v)/(2^|w|-M_w) and M_z); after canonicalization the residual
  gcd is small and the gains stay bounded (they are the partial-sum approximants in disguise).

