==============================================================================
  X_R = 1.0520245898011601445366354485065054080462396464408  (14 terms, 3000 digits)
  reliable partial quotients: 2700; max a_n = 3929; #a_n >= 100: 41 (Gauss-Kuzmin expects 38.7)
  Levy constant estimate log(q_n)/n = 1.1742 (typical: pi^2/(12 ln 2) = 1.1866)
  PSLQ, degree <= 6, coefficients <= 10^40 at 400 digits: None
  PSLQ on [1, X, X/1089, 33 X, 1/1089] (sanity: finds the trivial rational dependencies): [0, -33, 0, 1, 0]

==============================================================================
N4  2-adic X: denominators built from 1089, and the block length 33
==============================================================================
  for d = 1089^j, 33^j, 11^j, 121^j, 3^j (j < 60): the balanced residue of d X mod 2^N has >= 99989 bits (N = 100000), so X != c/d for every integer c with |c| < 2^99988.
  (Rational reconstruction in the previous note already excludes every a/b with |a|,|b| <= 2^4999999.)
  Block length 33 of the HYP-9131 word enters only through mu_bar = 23 log2(5)/33; Theorem H1 proves
  the word irrational for every L with mu_bar < 7/4, so '33' plays no role in the proof.

